WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.622
Sometimes a direct cast is sufficient If the text is
already in

00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:10.846
a clear date format that PostgreSQL recognizes and
you have validated the input casting to

00:00:10.859 --> 00:00:16.548
date can be simple When the format is different
TO_DATE lets

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:22.396
you specify the pattern For mixed raw input first
identify the shape

00:00:22.409 --> 00:00:27.942
and then apply the appropriate parser Blindly
parsing unknown text can

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:30.455
cause errors or incorrect interpretations
